# qwen3.8-27b-tf-nodraft on a Mac: qwen3.8-27b-tf with --no-drafts, the one change. Was:
# qwen3.8-27b-tf on a Mac: TensorFold 0.6.6 (MLX), Qwen3.8-27B dense, drafts on
# with z-lab's DFlash2 draft model. The most capable model of the -tf recipes
# (dense: all 27B weights work on every token), and TensorFold's best-tested
# Mac family; drafts are verified against the model's own greedy pick, so at
# temperature 0 they change speed, never the answer.
#
# 1 FIT     MLX 4-bit, groups of 64: 16.1 GB, plus the 3.8 GB draft model.
#           About 22 GB with a 65536-token window: fits from a 36 GB Mac.
WEIGHTS_GB=19.9
# 2 ENGINE  TensorFold at rack's pinned commit, in its own venv.
ENGINE=tensorfold
# 3 ACCESS  TensorFold's checkpoint and the draft model, both pinned (rack pull
#           fetches both; rack up passes the draft model as --drafter).
. "$RECIPE_DIR/model.env"
ARTIFACT=TensorFold/Qwen3.8-27B-MLX-4bit
ARTIFACT_REVISION=22d8d538154e0e5b6f8dcb1fcc74a60a0798104c
DRAFTER=z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2
DRAFTER_REVISION=50307d4c4cde6860d4eee73e2547cd786fe8e8a4
SERVE_ARGS=(
  # 4 SHAPE   rack up sets --host, --port, --name, --api-key-file, --drafter, --no-update-check.
  --context 65536
  --parallel 4
  --no-drafts                    # the one change from the -tf recipe
  # 6 SPEED   --no-drafts: one token a round (the serial reference, same output)
)
ENV_EXTRA=()
# 8 PROOF   not yet benched: rack up qwen3.8-27b-tf --mac && rack bench qwen3.8-27b-tf-nodraft
